    {
      "context_id": "CTX292_ESCAPE",
      "version": 1,
      "statement": "Audit the ordinary-sequence escape bound in nuclear-finiteness.tex for arbitrary unitary tuples in nonzero unital complex nuclear C*-algebras, with no dimension or separability restrictions.",
      "definitions": {
        "gap": "For nonempty finite generating S and 0<kappa<=4|S|, every unitary representation with no invariant vectors on any Hilbert space satisfies sum_s ||rho(s)v-v||^2 >= kappa||v||^2.",
        "L": "L(z)=sum_s (z_s-1)^*(z_s-1); m=|S|; b=kappa^2/(4m).",
        "matching": "d(u,pi)=min spectrum L((u_s tensor conjugate(pi(s)))_s).",
        "nuclear": "Minimal and maximal C*-tensor norms agree with every second C*-algebra.",
        "sequence": "pi_j are pairwise inequivalent irreducible unitary representations on nonzero finite-dimensional spaces, with unrestricted dimensions."
      },
      "content_hash": "2d23acf2e37f34718a2e840c37579db08f27989afa5cc96f11591b5350f3eb9f"
    }
  ],
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim_id": "C9000292",
      "version": 1,
      "context": {
        "kind": "context",
        "subject_id": "CTX9000292",
        "content_hash": "7453c35705ec532d1a2fa4b862f5f3c3e1c34742537b99198382a53a8727996e"
      },
      "natural_statement": "Adversarially audit, verify, or refute OpenAI Manuscript Family 292 (Kirchberg's $`\\mathcal O_2`$ norm-ultrapower embedding problem.; papers: An explicit obstruction to nuclear norm-ultrapower embeddings; Lean status: Partially/Comparator formalized (lean/docs/292.md)): either (a) discover and certify an explicit mathematical flaw, sign/orientation error, counterexample to an intermediate lemma, or statement-fidelity/citation gap with a deterministic symbolic/computational certificate (`verify.py` + `exact_certificate.json`), or (b) independently verify, repair, or generalize the manuscript's core mathematical theorem with a standalone machine-checkable certificate certified by the independent Reviewer.",
      "formal_statement": "",
      "external_assumptions": [],
      "retired_assumptions": [],
      "content_hash": "59d67570d7e8832f302da44eb4d1652e1deb999b3540708f21d98dbe1f5e944a"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "C292_MAIN",
      "version": 1,
      "context": {
        "kind": "context",
        "subject_id": "CTX9000292",
        "content_hash": "7453c35705ec532d1a2fa4b862f5f3c3e1c34742537b99198382a53a8727996e"
      },
      "natural_statement": "For G=Z[1/2]^3 semidirect (SL_3(Z) x Z), with (M,k) acting by 2^k M, C*(G) is separable and unital and has no unital embedding into B^omega for any nonzero unital nuclear B and any free ultrafilter omega on N. Source: thm:main; not verified in this bounded mission.",
      "formal_statement": "",
      "external_assumptions": [],
      "retired_assumptions": [],
      "content_hash": "ecd18beec9a7fa4b8d821f2b213333c56e38029ad6a09fe375ceb2ee2aede09c"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "C292_GROUP",
      "version": 1,
      "context": {
        "kind": "context",
        "subject_id": "CTX9000292",
        "content_hash": "7453c35705ec532d1a2fa4b862f5f3c3e1c34742537b99198382a53a8727996e"
      },
      "natural_statement": "Gamma=Z^3 semidirect SL_3(Z) is finitely generated with property (T); theta(v,M)=(2v,M) is an injective index-eight endomorphism implemented in G by conjugation; an irreducible pi_* factoring modulo 2 and nontrivial on translations is inequivalent to every positive theta-pullback. Source: lem:group-data; outside this bounded proof.",
      "formal_statement": "",
      "external_assumptions": [],
      "retired_assumptions": [],
      "content_hash": "39b1ac0fbd246c9c779d557268c5259e422955383a0d6cd7c1dfed3211beeb40"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "C292_SPECTRAL",
      "version": 1,
      "context": {
        "kind": "context",
        "subject_id": "CTX292_ESCAPE",
        "content_hash": "2d23acf2e37f34718a2e840c37579db08f27989afa5cc96f11591b5350f3eb9f"
      },
      "natural_statement": "For a genuine unitary group representation in a nonzero unital C*-algebra, the Laplacian spectrum is contained in {0} union [kappa,4|S|]; tensoring with conjugate pi detects occurrence of the finite-dimensional irreducible pi. Source: lem:spectral-gap and eq:matching-distance.",
      "formal_statement": "",
      "external_assumptions": [],
      "retired_assumptions": [],
      "content_hash": "e76eb292774a94d9e8d9aea1f9150fa4a975a9af369bb5c35294b9ade4396503"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "C292_SQRT",
      "version": 1,
      "context": {
        "kind": "context",
        "subject_id": "CTX292_ESCAPE",
        "content_hash": "2d23acf2e37f34718a2e840c37579db08f27989afa5cc96f11591b5350f3eb9f"
      },
      "natural_statement": "For positive Hilbert-Schmidt operators X,Y on any, possibly nonseparable, Hilbert space, ||X-Y||_2^2 <= ||X^2-Y^2||_1. Source: lem:square-root-trace.",
      "formal_statement": "",
      "external_assumptions": [],
      "retired_assumptions": [],
      "content_hash": "52e884f7e660041b958d5c323c99973cd5066e1aea9a66ba83fa8efda1d911ee"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "C292_WEAK",
      "version": 1,
      "context": {
        "kind": "context",
        "subject_id": "CTX292_ESCAPE",
        "content_hash": "2d23acf2e37f34718a2e840c37579db08f27989afa5cc96f11591b5350f3eb9f"
      },
      "natural_statement": "For every unitary sigma:Gamma->U(K) with no nonzero finite-dimensional subrepresentation, every Hilbert space E, and arbitrary unitaries U_s on E, L((U_s tensor sigma(s))_s) >= b times the identity, where b=kappa^2/(4|S|). No group relations among U_s are required. Source: lem:weak-mixing-bound.",
      "formal_statement": "",
      "external_assumptions": [],
      "retired_assumptions": [],
      "content_hash": "7ecd43d3592f8b8f863f5165c6d20d8d42ea97fe0f4070e164f54f18e240a841"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "C292_CORONA",
      "version": 1,
      "context": {
        "kind": "context",
        "subject_id": "CTX292_ESCAPE",
        "content_hash": "2d23acf2e37f34718a2e840c37579db08f27989afa5cc96f11591b5350f3eb9f"
      },
      "natural_statement": "Let Q=product_j B(conjugate V_pi_j)/c0 and q(g)=[conjugate pi_j(g)]. For every unital representation eta of Q on a Hilbert space, eta composed with q has no nonzero finite-dimensional subrepresentation. Source: the exclusion argument inside lem:nuclear-finiteness.",
      "formal_statement": "",
      "external_assumptions": [],
      "retired_assumptions": [],
      "content_hash": "963627e49c73fe898d538d559c85184cc5b1e5086f6e6053db54005c2e0a2ec6"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "C292_TRANSFER",
      "version": 1,
      "context": {
        "kind": "context",
        "subject_id": "CTX292_ESCAPE",
        "content_hash": "2d23acf2e37f34718a2e840c37579db08f27989afa5cc96f11591b5350f3eb9f"
      },
      "natural_statement": "For nonzero unital nuclear B and the matrix corona Q, the commuting maps alpha(x)=[x tensor 1] and beta([y_j])=[1 tensor y_j] induce a unital star-homomorphism Psi:B tensor_min Q -> product_j(B tensor M_j)/c0 sending x tensor [y_j] to [x tensor y_j]. Source: the nuclear tensor-product step inside lem:nuclear-finiteness.",
      "formal_statement": "",
      "external_assumptions": [],
      "retired_assumptions": [],
      "content_hash": "fa90b0469bbc11185b0df7af78d91bae1f73c5daa3818c8e76a86a66cf7cc403"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "C292_ESCAPE",
      "version": 1,
      "context": {
        "kind": "context",
        "subject_id": "CTX292_ESCAPE",
        "content_hash": "2d23acf2e37f34718a2e840c37579db08f27989afa5cc96f11591b5350f3eb9f"
      },
      "natural_statement": "For every nonzero unital nuclear B, every arbitrary unitary S-tuple u in B, and every sequence of pairwise inequivalent nonzero finite-dimensional irreducible unitary representations pi_j, liminf_j d(u,pi_j) >= kappa^2/(4|S|). Representation dimensions are unrestricted; B need not be separable; u need not satisfy any group relations. Source: final functional-calculus argument of lem:nuclear-finiteness.",
      "formal_statement": "",
      "external_assumptions": [],
      "retired_assumptions": [],
      "content_hash": "be31609f700c957b5ca4a8a379c4929578ddc8f00d432f88f1c202c27d05cd81"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "C292_FINITE",
      "version": 1,
      "context": {
        "kind": "context",
        "subject_id": "CTX292_ESCAPE",
        "content_hash": "2d23acf2e37f34718a2e840c37579db08f27989afa5cc96f11591b5350f3eb9f"
      },
      "natural_statement": "For any arbitrary unitary tuple u in a nonzero unital nuclear B and any real a<b, the set of equivalence classes of nonzero finite-dimensional irreducible pi with d(u,pi)<a is finite. This includes the manuscript threshold 0<a<min(kappa,b). Source: lem:nuclear-finiteness.",
      "formal_statement": "",
      "external_assumptions": [],
      "retired_assumptions": [],
      "content_hash": "44c018ae7a02ac85be61b6cb886efc03d1a50da8ced3bdcb725e0b3eba291c9a"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "C292_VARYING",
      "version": 1,
      "context": {
        "kind": "context",
        "subject_id": "CTX9000292",
        "content_hash": "7453c35705ec532d1a2fa4b862f5f3c3e1c34742537b99198382a53a8727996e"
      },
      "natural_statement": "In the putative ultrapower-embedding setup, every sequence of nonzero finite-dimensional representations pi_n, with unrestricted dimensions, satisfies lim_omega d(x_n,pi_n) in {0} union [kappa,4|S|]. Source: lem:varying-gap; outside this bounded proof.",
      "formal_statement": "",
      "external_assumptions": [],
      "retired_assumptions": [],
      "content_hash": "15dd870fcd7074e090435f3eef76010a40e40490a3d0109635f01c3af108896d"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "C292_INITIAL",
      "version": 1,
      "context": {
        "kind": "context",
        "subject_id": "CTX9000292",
        "content_hash": "7453c35705ec532d1a2fa4b862f5f3c3e1c34742537b99198382a53a8727996e"
      },
      "natural_statement": "In the putative faithful ultrapower-embedding setup, lim_omega d(x_n,pi_*)=0, so pi_* belongs to D_n on an ultrafilter-large set. Source: lem:initial-match; outside this bounded proof.",
      "formal_statement": "",
      "external_assumptions": [],
      "retired_assumptions": [],
      "content_hash": "02422c73b836d004b094037fd3bcff861c05dbf6e0deae9050af53935168f7d6"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "C292_PREDECESSOR",
      "version": 1,
      "context": {
        "kind": "context",
        "subject_id": "CTX9000292",
        "content_hash": "7453c35705ec532d1a2fa4b862f5f3c3e1c34742537b99198382a53a8727996e"
      },
      "natural_statement": "In the putative ultrapower-embedding setup, on one ultrafilter-large set of coordinates n, every pi in D_n has a pi_prime in D_n with pi occurring in pi_prime composed with theta. Source: lem:uniform-predecessor; outside this bounded proof.",
      "formal_statement": "",
      "external_assumptions": [],
      "retired_assumptions": [],
      "content_hash": "1f95d35ac94e4965cf1d9d80a6d7cd72e1569ad3c3f15473ffa58a7bf1f9f7a1"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "C292_CYCLE",
      "version": 1,
      "context": {
        "kind": "context",
        "subject_id": "CTX9000292",
        "content_hash": "7453c35705ec532d1a2fa4b862f5f3c3e1c34742537b99198382a53a8727996e"
      },
      "natural_statement": "For any group homomorphism theta and finite set D of equivalence classes of nonzero finite-dimensional irreducible unitary representations, if each pi in D occurs in pi_prime composed with theta for some pi_prime in D, then each pi in D is equivalent to pi composed with theta^p for some integer p>=1. Source: lem:finite-predecessor-cycle; outside this bounded proof.",
      "formal_statement": "",
      "external_assumptions": [],
      "retired_assumptions": [],
      "content_hash": "20b1c77aa34bf05dcff215daedce2d39c4acb0e7eb42a98563bbfc7e84e0f1f4"
    },
    {
