        "content_hash": "2d23acf2e37f34718a2e840c37579db08f27989afa5cc96f11591b5350f3eb9f"
      },
      "natural_statement": "For nonzero unital nuclear B and the matrix corona Q, the commuting maps alpha(x)=[x tensor 1] and beta([y_j])=[1 tensor y_j] induce a unital star-homomorphism Psi:B tensor_min Q -> product_j(B tensor M_j)/c0 sending x tensor [y_j] to [x tensor y_j]. Source: the nuclear tensor-product step inside lem:nuclear-finiteness.",
      "formal_statement": "",
      "external_assumptions": [
        {
          "assumption_id": "A292_NUCLEAR_NORM",
          "statement": "A nuclear C*-algebra B has a unique compatible C*-tensor norm on B algebraic-tensor C for every C; in particular the spatial and maximal completions agree canonically. This is the tensor-norm definition of nuclearity used here.",
          "source": "Takesaki, On the cross-norm of the direct product of C*-algebras (1964), p.111 condition (T).",
          "source_id": "doi:10.2748/tmj/1178243737",
